course: dictionary
lesson: 7101
title: The peahen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A peahen is a female peafowl. Read the clues around the word: «Asian forests have great hornbills, peacocks and golden pheasants; peahens choose males with the best tails of eye spots.» The peahen is the bird that chooses, and the peacock is the one with the showy tail.
explain: Look at the word parts. Peacock is the male, and hen means a female bird, so peahen is the female. Check it by swapping the words: if the peacock grows a huge tail, then the peahen is the one without it.
explain: Many people say peacock for both birds, but that is not correct. A female is always a peahen, and the babies are called peachicks.
fact: A peahen is a female peafowl.
fact: She is mostly brown and grey, without the huge colourful tail of the male peacock.
fact: Her dull colours help her hide while she sits on her eggs.
fact: The male peacock shows off his bright tail to attract peahens.
fact: The babies of a peahen are called peachicks.
exercise: «Asian forests have great hornbills, peacocks and golden pheasants; peahens choose males with the best tails of eye spots.» What is a peahen? | A kind of golden pheasant | A baby peafowl | A male peacock with a huge tail | *A female peafowl
exercise: Why are peahens mostly brown and grey? | To show off to other birds | To look like the male peacock | To be seen from far away | *To hide while sitting on their eggs
exercise: What are the babies of a peahen called? | Peafledges | Hens | Peacubs | *Peachicks
test:
Which bird has the huge colourful tail that the peahen does not have? | Peahen | *Peacock | Hornbill | Pheasant
Ella says the female bird is a peacock. What is the correct word? | Peacock | *Peahen | Peachick | Golden pheasant
exam:
A peahen sits quietly in the forest on her eggs. Why are her colours so dull? | To attract a peacock | *To help her hide | To show off her tail | To scare away the hornbills
